    "body": "still this issue,\n\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 229, in benchmark\n[rank80]: timings = {config: self._bench(*args, config=config, **kwargs) for config in pruned_configs}\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 164, in _bench\n[rank80]: return self.do_bench(kernel_call, quantiles=(0.5, 0.2, 0.8))\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/testing.py\", line 149, in do_bench\n[rank80]: fn()\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 150, in kernel_call\n[rank80]: self.fn.run(\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/runtime/jit.py\", line 720, in run\n[rank80]: kernel = self._do_compile(key, signature, device, constexprs, options, attrs, warmup)\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/runtime/jit.py\", line 849, in _do_compile\n[rank80]: kernel = self.compile(src, target=target, options=options.dict)\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/compiler/compiler.py\", line 360, in compile\n[rank80]: return CompiledKernel(src, metadata_group, hash)\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/site-packages/triton/compiler/compiler.py\", line 424, in init\n[rank80]: file.suffix[1:]: file.read_bytes() if file.suffix[1:] == binary_ext else file.read_text()\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/pathlib.py\", line 1027, in read_text\n[rank80]: with self.open(mode='r', encoding=encoding, errors=errors) as f:\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: File \"/mnt/afs/miniconda3/envs/test_train/lib/python3.12/pathlib.py\", line 1013, in open\n[rank80]: return io.open(self, mode, buffering, encoding, errors, newline)\n[rank80]: ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n[rank80]: FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/mnt/afs/multimodal_ckpt/node_cache_256/triton_cache/node_rank_10/HVKQBUPFRA2XX66OCAMFFO5VJPC6FGL46SMTFLDJ7CRNCNI2BPHA/l2norm_fwd_kernel.llir'\n\nIn my case, I use TRITON_CACHE_DIR=.../node_rank_${node_rank} to avoid Triton's multinode cache writing. But the issue persists, seemingly due to multi-rank interrupts in a single node.",
